.TH SESSLINT 1 "" "SessLint 0.3.0" "SessLint Manual"
.SH NAME
sesslint \- offline, vendor-neutral session integrity checker and conservative repair tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sesslint
[\-\-color auto|always|never] [\-\-profile PROFILE] <command> [<args>]
.SH DESCRIPTION
SessLint inspects AI agent session ledgers (Claude Code JSONL,
OpenAI Agents exports, Codex rollout streams, and the canonical
sesslint.session/v1 format) for structural and integrity defects,
and can conservatively repair a bounded set of them. It runs fully
offline with zero runtime dependencies, produces content-free
findings by default, and fails closed whenever repair safety cannot
be proven.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B baseline
[read\-only] Upgrade a v1 baseline to the path\-normalized v2 format.
.TP
.B bundle
[read\-only] Generate a privacy\-safe diagnostic support bundle and fixture skeleton.
.TP
.B check
[read\-only] Check a session file with auto\-detection.
.TP
.B completion
[read\-only] Print shell completion script.
.TP
.B diff
[read\-only] Structurally diff two session files.
.TP
.B doctor
[read\-only] Environment diagnostics for support reports.
.TP
.B export
[writes: output file] Export a session artifact to canonical format for repair.
.TP
.B formats
[read\-only] List supported session format adapters.
.TP
.B init\-hooks
[read\-only] Print ready\-to\-merge agent hook snippets (never writes config).
.TP
.B mcp
[read\-only] Run a Model Context Protocol server over stdio.
.TP
.B repair
[writes: output file and manifest, lossy under \-\-policy salvage] Safely repair a session file.
.TP
.B scan
[read\-only] Scan directory trees for session artifacts or display limits.
.TP
.B stats
[read\-only] Aggregate content\-free statistics over session files.
.TP
.B validate\-session
[read\-only] Validate a canonical session file against schema.
.TP
.B verify
[read\-only] Verify integrity, hash bindings, and idempotence of a repaired session.
.TP
.B version
[read\-only] Display detailed component and schema version information.
.TP
.B watch
[read\-only] Poll session directories and flag newly corrupted files.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-profile PROFILE
Replay validation profile (default: neutral).
.TP
.B \-\-color auto|always|never
Control colored terminal output (default: auto).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable ANSI color styling (equivalent to NO_COLOR=1).
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B .sesslint.toml / pyproject.toml [tool.sesslint]
Optional configuration file and section.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success — clean check, or repair executed, validated, and manifested.
.TP
.B 1
Finding / refusal — diagnostic errors found, repair plan blocked, or
execution refused (TOCTOU, SL203).
.TP
.B 2
Operational error — CLI syntax error, file not found, permission denied,
or live-DB path refusal.
.TP
.B 130
Cancelled — interrupted via Ctrl+C or a cooperative cancellation request;
partial outputs are cleaned up.
.SH SEE ALSO
sesslint\-baseline(1), sesslint\-bundle(1), sesslint\-check(1), sesslint\-completion(1), sesslint\-diff(1), sesslint\-doctor(1), sesslint\-export(1), sesslint\-formats(1).

.nf
Full documentation: the docs/ tree in the source repository
